DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 13

Terraform (Basics + Advanced) | 0–2 Years Experience

Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is a must-have skill for modern DevOps engineers.
Terraform helps you provision, version, and manage infrastructure safely and repeatedly.

 Focus: Terraform Interview Questions (Basics + Advanced)

• What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC)?
• What is Terraform and why is it used?
• Terraform vs CloudFormation vs ARM (high-level)
• What is a provider in Terraform?
• What is a resource?
• What is a data source?
• Terraform workflow (init, plan, apply, destroy)
• What is Terraform state?
• Why is state important?
• Local state vs remote state
• What is state locking?
• What is backend in Terraform?
• What is a variable in Terraform?
• Difference between var, tfvars, and environment variables
• What is output in Terraform?
• What is dependency in Terraform?
• Implicit vs explicit dependency

🔹 Advanced Terraform Concepts (Beginner-Friendly)
• What are Terraform modules?
• Why are modules used?
• How do you create reusable modules?
• What are workspaces?
• When do you use Terraform workspaces?
• What is terraform import?
• What is terraform taint?
• What is terraform refresh?
• How do you manage secrets in Terraform?
• How do you secure Terraform state?
